# Proposed controller tuning log

Date: 2026-11-10
Branch: jturn-current
Repository: JiaMingXu2482/PMPC

## Condition

- CarSim dataset: `Run_4d669775-9558-4a06-a4ef-d6a3994def34`
- Run control: `DLC80_mu0.5_PMPC`, vehicle `i_i`
- Initial speed: 80 km/h, target 80 km/h
- Road: DLC mu=0.5 split-friction test pad (0.5 inside the DLC area)
- TSTOP: 10 s
- Reference: original tanh DLC path in `pmpc_init` case 1

## Controller parameters

| Controller | Q_epsi | R2 | slack / caps | Other |
|---|---:|---:|---|---|
| MPC-NPC | 20 | 200 | `[0.5e4;0.5e4;1e4;1e4]` | fixed weights |
| ZENG | 10 | 200 | `slack=1e4` | `rho_I0=1.0`, `rho_dI=0.3` |
| Proposed | 10 | 200 | `w2_max=w1_max=2e3` | `Wb=100`, `w2_gain=w1_gain=3` |

The MPC and ZENG parameters are the version in
`PMPC_Results/DLC_mu0.5_80_compare/zeng_tuned_vs_mpc.png`.

## Proposed tuning sweep

Fixed: `Q_epsi=10`, `Wb=100`, `gain=3`, `R2=200`.

| w2_max / w1_max | ey max | ey RMS | SW max | QP |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 1e6 / 1e5 (original) | 0.792 | 0.379 | 358.1 deg | 99.5% |
| 1e4 / 1e4 | 0.695 | 0.326 | 362.6 deg | 100% |
| **2e3 / 2e3 (selected)** | **0.674** | **0.272** | **88.6 deg** | **100%** |
| 1e3 / 1e3 | 0.698 | 0.268 | 87.2 deg | 100% |
| 500 / 500 | 0.731 | 0.270 | 90.6 deg | 100% |

The original caps allowed the online weights to reach `1e6/1e5` near
`margin -> 0`, causing QP active-set chattering, large steering, `Mz`
oscillation, and occasional QP failure. Capping the weights at `2e3`
regularized the QP and let the controller allocate yaw/roll effort to
`Mz/Md` instead of steering.

`Wb` (1/10/100) and `w2_gain/w1_gain` (1/3/5) had little effect once the
caps were at `1e3-2e3`; the cap is the dominant knob.

## Final three-controller result

| Controller | ey max | ey RMS | ey final | SW max | Mz max | Md max | beta max | yaw max | LTR max | QP |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| MPC-NPC | 0.805 | 0.363 | 0.097 | 396.1 | 2778 | 1325 | 1.72 | 13.1 | 0.48 | 100% |
| ZENG | 0.689 | 0.316 | 0.084 | 320.5 | 2815 | 1710 | 1.79 | 14.9 | 0.48 | 100% |
| **Proposed tuned** | **0.674** | **0.272** | **0.031** | **88.6** | **2729** | **1152** | **1.40** | 13.1 | **0.44** | **100%** |

All quantities except QP are lower-is-better. SW/Mz/Md units: deg and N*m;
beta: deg; yaw: deg/s.

## Improvement of Proposed vs baselines

Formula: `(baseline - proposed) / baseline * 100%`; positive is better.

| Metric | vs MPC | vs ZENG |
|---|---:|---:|
| ey max | +16.27% | +2.18% |
| ey RMS | +25.07% | +13.92% |
| SW max | +77.63% | +72.36% |
| Mz max | +1.76% | +3.06% |
| Md max | +13.06% | +32.63% |
| beta max | +18.60% | +21.79% |
| yaw max | 0.00% | +12.08% |
| LTR max | +8.33% | +8.33% |
| QP | equal (100%) | equal (100%) |

Before tuning, Proposed was `ey 1.556/0.676`, `SW 500.7 deg`, `QP 98.9%`.
After tuning it is `ey 0.674/0.272`, `SW 88.6 deg`, `QP 100%`.

## Verification and reproduction

The tuned values are now defaults in `pmpc_core/pmpc_init.m`:

```matlab
M.Wb = 100;
M.w2_max = 2e3;
M.w2_gain = 3;
M.w1_max = 2e3;
M.w1_gain = 3;
% DLC + controller 3
M.Q_norm(6) = 10;
M.R_norm(2) = 200;
```

Default check:

```matlab
dlc_one(1e4,10,'prop_default_check',3,80)
```

Result: `ey max 0.674`, `ey RMS 0.272`, `QP 100%` — identical to the
selected sweep point `prop_cap2k`.

