## Notes

- Proposed uses only about 4.6 deg front-wheel steering (`Steer_L1`) and
  performs the turn mainly with `Mz/Md`; `LTR` is lower (0.44 vs 0.48), so
  this is not achieved by relaxing the roll constraint.
- The ZENG 14.4% max / 12.9% RMS result is relative to the MPC baseline
  with `Q_epsi=20`. If MPC is also retuned to `Q_epsi=10`, MPC reaches
  `0.650/0.311`; this caveat must be stated in the paper.
- `2e3/2e3` is tuned at DLC 80 km/h, mu=0.5. Recheck before using the same
  Proposed caps on J-turn/Slalom or other speeds.
